From 3d9478df1f371a472b154466714743fb3cf9ed0d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sebastian Huang <sebastian_huang@accton.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 20:02:15 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] mtk: mt76: mt7915: use the full TX token pool without WED

The SDK sets the software TX token pool of mt7915 to
MT7915_WED_SW_TOKEN_SIZE (1024) for all devices. That size is meant for
WED, where most of the traffic uses the WED token range and only the
remaining frames take software tokens. Without WED every frame takes a
software token, and the pool of 1024, shared by both bands, ran out
thousands of times a minute on the EAP111 with tens of clients:

  txtoken: pool exhausted, TX queues stopped (#2241): in use 960/1024, band0 960, band1 0

Use MT7915_TOKEN_SIZE (8192) when WED is not active, as upstream does.
mt76_wed_offload_enable/disable(), which reset the size, only run with
WED.
---
 mt7915/init.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/mt7915/init.c b/mt7915/init.c
index 4300d66c..3c04cfec 100644
--- a/mt7915/init.c
+++ b/mt7915/init.c
@@ -1317,6 +1317,13 @@ int mt7915_register_device(struct mt7915_dev *dev)
 
 	dev->dbdc_support = mt7915_band_config(dev);
 
+	/* The software TX token pool is sized for WED, which carries most of
+	 * the traffic in its own token range. Without WED all TX goes through
+	 * the software pool, so give it the full size, as upstream does.
+	 */
+	if (!mtk_wed_device_active(&dev->mt76.mmio.wed))
+		dev->mt76.token_size = MT7915_TOKEN_SIZE;
+
 	phy2 = mt7915_alloc_ext_phy(dev);
 	if (IS_ERR(phy2))
 		return PTR_ERR(phy2);
-- 
